Today, CHY3 is open to the public.

Six months ago it was a note in Notion, built around a question we could not stop asking: why is the toolchain for independent creators so fragmented? Open source has transformed developer tools. It has barely touched the economics of creative work.

# Two answers to start

The first two projects represent two halves of the problem. IdeaForge answers “where do I begin?” — AI-assisted ideation and rapid prototyping make the first version cheap enough to test. ValueFlow answers “what is working?” — end-to-end analytics make every step from idea to revenue visible. Together they form a loop from incubation to data-driven iteration.

# Open source is a commitment, not a license

Every project is released under Apache 2.0. Governance follows a public RFC process, and roadmap discussions happen in GitHub Discussions. The code is the minimum. The real commitment is that decisions, disagreements, and trade-offs are visible to the people who depend on the tools.

# Thank you

To the 100+ alpha testers who gave feedback before there was anything polished: this is your launch too. CHY3 is at the beginning. We are looking for creators and developers who want to redefine how creative work creates value.
